.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.COMMON.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.common.mk
.Nd target selection, target key and flags shared by every role
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read first by every role file.
It works out the target and toolchain, reads the toolchain's file, builds the
target key and sets the common flags.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Ss Target selection
.Bl -tag -width "TARGET_ARCH"
.It Va TARGET
The operating system:
.Cm macos , linux , freebsd , netbsd
or
.Cm win .
Default: the host's.
.It Va TARGET_ARCH
.Cm amd64
or
.Cm arm64 .
Default: the host's.
.It Va TOOLCHAIN
.Cm llvm ,
the default,
.Cm gcc
or
.Cm msvc .
.It Va ABI
Only where a target has several runtimes:
Linux
.Cm glibc
or
.Cm musl ;
Windows
.Cm msvc , mingw
or
.Cm cygwin .
On a Cygwin host,
.Cm llvm
or
.Cm gcc
alone give Cygwin output,
.Va ABI Ns = Ns Cm mingw
native mingw-w64 output, and
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm llvm Va ABI Ns = Ns Cm msvc
the MSVC runtime with clang.
A combination that cannot exist is an error.
.El
.Ss Set for you
.Bl -tag -width "SHAREDIR_LOCAL"
.It Va OS_ARCH
The target key,
.Ar os Ns - Ns Ar arch Ns Op - Ns Ar toolchain Ns Op - Ns Ar abi .
.It Va BUILD_ROOT
.Pa build/ Ns Va OS_ARCH
.It Va DISTRIB_ROOT
.Pa distrib/ Ns Va OS_ARCH
.It Va OBJDIR , Va BINDIR_LOCAL , Va LIBDIR_LOCAL , Va INCDIR_LOCAL , Va SHAREDIR_LOCAL
.Pa obj , bin , lib , include
and
.Pa share
under
.Va BUILD_ROOT .
.It Va BMK_IS_NATIVE_BUILD
.Cm yes
unless cross-compiling.
.It Va BMK_MKDIR
The directory of these files.
.It Va NATIVE_CURDIR
The module's directory in a form the program being built can open:
.Pa C:/...
for native Windows output on a Cygwin host, otherwise
.Va .CURDIR .
For a path compiled into a program:
.Dl CFLAGS += -DDATA='\(dq${NATIVE_CURDIR}/data\(dq'
.El
.Ss Flags
.Bl -tag -width "INPUTS_HASH_EXTRA"
.It Va CFLAGS , Va CXXFLAGS , Va LDFLAGS , Va YFLAGS , Va LFLAGS
Append with
.Ql += .
A change rebuilds what they affect.
.It Va DEBUG_FLAGS
Usually
.Fl g .
.It Va CXXSTD
The C++ standard.
Default
.Cm c++17 .
.It Va WARN
.Cm none
silences this module's warnings, for compiling third-party source.
Otherwise
.Fl Wall Fl Wextra .
.It Va OPENMP
.Cm yes
builds with OpenMP.
Default
.Cm no .
A compiler that cannot is an error.
.It Va SANITIZE
A comma-separated list of
.Cm address , undefined , thread , memory
and
.Cm leak ,
in which
.Cm address , thread
and
.Cm memory
exclude one another.
MSVC has only
.Cm address .
.It Va INPUTS_HASH_EXTRA
Anything else whose change must rebuild the module.
.El
.Ss Runs and reports
.Bl -tag -width "FAIL_FAST"
.It Va REPORT
.Cm yes :
also build the dashboard of a workspace or framework
.Cm all
or
.Cm test .
Logs are written either way.
.It Va FAIL_FAST
.Cm yes :
stop at the first failed module.
By default the rest still run, and the exit status reports the failure.
.It Va RUN_ID
Names this run's logs and reports.
Default: a timestamp and process id.
Set it to correlate with a CI build number.
.El
.Ss Targets
.Bl -tag -width "run"
.It Cm run
.Va PROGRAM Ns = Ns Ar name Op Va ARGS Ns = Ns Ar args
runs a program through the build environment, from any directory of the
workspace: the workspace's and each parent's
.Pa bin
are prepended to
.Ev PATH ,
their
.Pa lib
to the library search variable, and
.Ev BMK_BINDIR , BMK_LIBDIR , BMK_SHAREDIR , BMK_TARGET
and
.Ev BMK_LIBVAR
are set.
It does not build.
.Va PROGRAM Ns = Ns Cm sh
opens a shell in that environment.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The variables above may come from the environment, the command line or a hook
file, by the usual
.Xr make 1
precedence.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "build/KEY/runs/RUN_ID/build.log"
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /runs/ Ns Ar RUN_ID Ns Pa /build.log
one run's output
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /runs/latest/
a copy of the newest run
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ bmake TARGET=linux TARGET_ARCH=arm64
$ bmake ABI=mingw TOOLCHAIN=gcc
$ bmake test SANITIZE=address,undefined
$ bmake all REPORT=yes RUN_ID=ci-4821
$ bmake run PROGRAM=viewer ARGS="--title 'my scene' f.las"
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It ABI= Ns Ar abi contradicts this build
The compiler produces another runtime than the one asked for.
.It ABI=msvc with TOOLCHAIN=gcc
gcc does not build for the MSVC runtime.
.El
An unknown
.Va TOOLCHAIN
is an error listing those that exist, and which one a common alias means.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.local.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.gcc.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.llvm.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.msvc.mk 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
